WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.820
Welcome to Organizational Training. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Build the capabilities needed to perform organizational processes.

2
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:20.200
Consider this scenario. Developers receive a new process but no practical training. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:29.890
Start with two steps: Identify skill requirements. Then Plan targeted training. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:38.990
Continue with Provide guided practice. Then Evaluate on-the-job competence. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:59.360
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous competency needs, learning records, workplace evaluation tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: counting course attendance as demonstrated competence; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:13.610
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
